    "body": "### Motivation & Background\n\nCurrently, the libbitcoinkernel C API does not provide a way to configure block pruning on \btck_ChainstateManagerOptions. Even though the underlying \node::BlockManager::Options and \node::ChainstateLoadOptions structures support pruning, libbitcoinkernel callers cannot pass a prune target.\n\nConsequently, trying to open an existing pruned node's data directory fails during \node::LoadChainstate() with:\n``\n[error] Failed to load chain state from your data directory: You need to rebuild the database using -reindex to go back to unpruned mode.\n``\nbecause chainman.m_blockman.m_have_pruned is true while options.prune defaults to false.\n\n### Description of Changes\n\n1. **C API (src/kernel/bitcoinkernel.h)**:\n   - Added \btck_chainstate_manager_options_set_prune_target(opts, prune_target_bytes).\n   - Exposed \btck_PRUNE_TARGET_MANUAL (matching \node::BlockManager::PRUNE_TARGET_MANUAL) for manual pruning (-prune=1).\n   - Exposed \btck_MIN_PRUNE_TARGET_BYTES (550 MiB, matching MIN_DISK_SPACE_FOR_BLOCK_FILES).\n\n2. **Kernel Implementation (src/kernel/bitcoinkernel.cpp)**:\n   - Implemented \btck_chainstate_manager_options_set_prune_target().\n   - Validates that prune_target_bytes is either 0 (unpruned), \btck_PRUNE_TARGET_MANUAL, or >= btck_MIN_PRUNE_TARGET_BYTES.\n   - Sets m_blockman_options.prune_target = prune_target_bytes and m_chainstate_load_options.prune = (prune_target_bytes > 0) under LOCK(opts.m_mutex).\n\n3. **C++ Wrapper & Tests**:\n   - Added SetPruneTarget() in src/kernel/bitcoinkernel_wrapper.h.\n   - Added boundary tests in src/test/kernel/test_kernel.cpp (verifying rejection of < 550_MiB, acceptance of minimum, manual, and unpruned values).\n\nFixes #35627.",
