      "body": "Could you revisit the discussion in [#35627](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/35627)? This PR exposes automatic pruning through `ChainstateManagerOptions`, while the storage-interface and application-retention concerns raised in the issue remain unresolved.\r\n\r\nThe added tests do not exercise the reported problem. They check four setter return values, then reset the target to 0 before constructing the chainstate manager. They therefore do not demonstrate that an existing pruned directory can be opened successfully, or that automatic pruning behaves correctly.",
